# ── Auto-fetched DDB party sheets (other players' data) ───────
# ddb_party_sync.js pulls full character sheets players shared only
# "Campaign Only" on D&D Beyond — republishing them to this PUBLIC repo
# would override that choice. Ignore the generated raw JSON + markdown.
# (The hand-written "<Name> - Character Sheet.md" files are NOT affected.)
03-Characters/01 PCs/Party Character Sheets/_raw/
03-Characters/01 PCs/Party Character Sheets/*(DDB).md

# SKILLS.md is generated by claude-artifacts/scripts/skill-usage-audit.ps1 and is
# deliberately NOT published from this repo, which is public. The file may exist
# locally; the cross-project record lives in the private septentrion vault at
# Skills/.system/SKILL-DISTRIBUTION.md. Ignored here so Obsidian Git cannot
# auto-commit it (that is exactly how it reached sitl_vault's public remote on
# 2026-09-27 before the publish decision was made).
SKILLS.md

# Screenshots of admin dashboards. This repo is PUBLIC, and a console capture can
# leak account IDs, game IDs, hostnames and config layout — on 2026-09-29 a
# Cloudflare capture in another vault had the account ID in the FILENAME alone, so
# checking the pixels is not enough. The privacy screen only reads
# .md/.json/.txt/.canvas/.base/.html, so images are invisible to it and Obsidian
# Git would auto-commit them on its timer. Media folders are tracked on purpose,
# so this is by filename pattern. Added 2026-10-01 under the archive note's
# privacy/security exception; nothing matching was tracked at the time.
screencapture-*
**/screencapture-*
*dash.cloudflare*

# 🛑 Ogre.png — ignored, NOT deleted; its fate is Taylor's call, same as the
# wtff_vault/ block below. 1.9 MB, dated 2026-06-09, sitting loose at the vault
# root and untracked ever since.
#
# WHY IT IS IGNORED RATHER THAN COMMITTED. This repo is PUBLIC and tracks ZERO
# images today, so committing it would both set a new convention and put an
# unscreenable binary into permanent history. The screenshot block above already
# records why that matters here: the privacy screen reads only
# .md/.json/.txt/.canvas/.base/.html, so an image is invisible to it, and a
# binary cannot be un-published by a later commit.
#
# It is very likely just a character portrait — "Ogre" is a party member and
# PP_18 is titled "Hi_Im_Ogre" — in which case it is harmless and belongs in
# 04-Assets or similar. But "very likely" is not the standard for a public repo,
# and the other four vaults DO track images (skitl 33, wtff 47, Dimension20 11,
# ashfall 2), so there is no fleet-wide rule to lean on either way.
#
# ▶ To resolve: look at it, then either delete this line and commit it to a
# proper media folder, or move it out of the repo. Added 2026-10-06 because the
# Stop guard counts it as unbanked work every session otherwise.
Ogre.png

# 🛑 wtff_vault/ is a near-duplicate copy of the WtFF vault left here from before
# that project was split into its own repo (2026-10-01). Ignored, NOT deleted: its
# fate is still Taylor's call, and it is untracked data.
#
# WHY THIS LINE EXISTS, because it is not obvious. That folder has its own .git,
# but that .git has no refs/ directory, which makes it an INVALID git dir, so git
# discovery WALKS UP and every git command run from inside it silently operates on
# pacts_power_vault instead. Its HANDOFF.md sat at exactly 15 entries against the
# rotation cap of 15; one more entry and the Handoff Log Rotate task (which scans
# two levels deep, so it enrols this folder) would have rewritten that file,
# staged it as wtff_vault/HANDOFF.md, and self-banked it straight into THIS PUBLIC
# repo as a routine-looking "chore: rotate HANDOFF.md log" commit.
#
# Ignoring it closes that route: `git add` on an ignored path fails without -f.
# It also stops audit-public attributing that folder's findings to this repo.
# 21 of its 24 top-level files are byte-identical to the real wtff_vault; the 3
# that differ (HANDOFF.md, TOOLS.md, .gitignore) are stale copies from 09-05,
# 09-02 and 08-24. Delete this block if the folder is ever resolved properly.
wtff_vault/
